  "reasoning": "For the 2026 U.S. Senate race, major outlets report Democrat James Talarico versus Republican Ken Paxton on the ballot.[11][20] A late-July Texas Public Opinion Research poll cited by the Texas Tribune and Yahoo News shows Talarico leading Paxton 45% to 40%, a 5\u2011point Democratic advantage, while a UT/Texas Politics poll has Paxton ahead 43% to 42%, indicating a very competitive race with mixed polling signals.[11][13] Cook Political Report still rates the Senate race as Lean Republican, but the same Texas Tribune piece and recent polls show Republicans only narrowly ahead in the governor\u2019s race (Abbott 45%\u201342% over Gina Hinojosa), reinforcing that statewide contests are currently close despite Texas\u2019s structural Republican advantage.[11][12] The statewide Cook Partisan Voting Index lists Texas at R+6, reflecting a baseline GOP lean even though current Senate polling slightly favors the Democrat.[1][8][12]",
